# ACK android17-6.18 UFS parent/reference supply patch sketch

Status: .draft source sketch; not a directly applicable git diff. The source
context was checked against public android17-6.18, but it has not been applied
to a pinned checkout, compiled, schema-validated or runtime-tested.

## Motivation

HOS4.3 fragment@64 places both qcom,vddp-ref-clk-supply (100 uA) and
qcom,vccq-parent-supply (210 mA) on the UFS Host node. The local DTS draft
must therefore put both consumer phandles under &ufs_mem_hc, not under
&ufs_mem_phy. ACK QMP UFS PHY's SM8250 regulator list contains only
vdda-phy and vdda-pll. The vendor VDDP REF_CLK pad rail is consumed by the
Qualcomm UFS Host variant driver, not by the generic QMP PHY provider.

## Proposed struct additions in drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.h

```c
struct regulator;

struct ufs_qcom_host {
	/* existing fields */
	struct regulator *vddp_ref_clk;
	u32 vddp_ref_clk_max_uA;
	bool vddp_ref_clk_enabled;
	struct regulator *vccq_parent;
	u32 vccq_parent_max_uA;
	bool vccq_parent_enabled;
};
```

## Proposed helper logic in drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c

Add linux/regulator/consumer.h. Use one common helper for the two optional
Qualcomm-specific regulator consumer properties:

```c
static void ufs_qcom_disable_optional_supply(struct ufs_qcom_host *host,
		struct regulator *reg, u32 max_uA, bool *enabled)
{
	int ret;

	if (!reg || !*enabled)
		return;

	if (max_uA) {
		ret = regulator_set_load(reg, 0);
		if (ret)
			dev_warn(host->hba->dev,
				 "failed to clear optional UFS supply load: %d\n", ret);
	}

	ret = regulator_disable(reg);
	if (ret) {
		dev_warn(host->hba->dev,
			 "failed to disable optional UFS supply: %d\n", ret);
		return;
	}

	*enabled = false;
}

static int ufs_qcom_enable_optional_supply(struct ufs_qcom_host *host,
		const char *supply_prop, const char *consumer_id,
		const char *max_load_prop, struct regulator **reg,
		u32 *max_uA, bool *enabled)
{
	struct device *dev = host->hba->dev;
	int err;

	if (!dev->of_node || !of_find_property(dev->of_node, supply_prop, NULL))
		return 0;

	err = of_property_read_u32(dev->of_node, max_load_prop, max_uA);
	if (err)
		return dev_err_probe(dev, err,
				     "missing optional UFS supply max-load property\n");

	*reg = devm_regulator_get_optional(dev, consumer_id);
	if (IS_ERR(*reg)) {
		err = PTR_ERR(*reg);
		*reg = NULL;
		return dev_err_probe(dev, err,
				     "failed to get optional UFS supply\n");
	}

	err = regulator_enable(*reg);
	if (err)
		return dev_err_probe(dev, err,
				     "failed to enable optional UFS supply\n");

	*enabled = true;
	if (*max_uA) {
		err = regulator_set_load(*reg, *max_uA);
		if (err) {
			ufs_qcom_disable_optional_supply(host, *reg, *max_uA, enabled);
			return dev_err_probe(dev, err,
					     "failed to vote optional UFS supply load\n");
		}
	}

	return 0;
}
```

## Proposed calls inside ufs_qcom_init()

After ufs_qcom_icc_init() succeeds and before UFS lane/link bring-up,
enable the reference-clock pad supply first, then the VCCQ parent supply:

```c
err = ufs_qcom_enable_optional_supply(host,
		"qcom,vddp-ref-clk-supply", "qcom,vddp-ref-clk",
		"qcom,vddp-ref-clk-max-microamp", &host->vddp_ref_clk,
		&host->vddp_ref_clk_max_uA, &host->vddp_ref_clk_enabled);
if (err)
	goto out_variant_clear;

err = ufs_qcom_enable_optional_supply(host,
		"qcom,vccq-parent-supply", "qcom,vccq-parent",
		"qcom,vccq-parent-max-microamp", &host->vccq_parent,
		&host->vccq_parent_max_uA, &host->vccq_parent_enabled);
if (err)
	goto out_variant_clear;
```

At out_variant_clear and in ufs_qcom_exit(), release in reverse order:

```c
ufs_qcom_disable_optional_supply(host, host->vccq_parent,
		host->vccq_parent_max_uA, &host->vccq_parent_enabled);
ufs_qcom_disable_optional_supply(host, host->vddp_ref_clk,
		host->vddp_ref_clk_max_uA, &host->vddp_ref_clk_enabled);
```

The sketch keeps both rails enabled while the UFS host is bound. It does not
guess link-off suspend/resume policy. Downstream Qualcomm variants gate VDDP
and VCCQ-parent differently based on link state and BKOPS; the exact HOS4.3
implementation is not available in this source review.

## Binding additions in Documentation/devicetree/bindings/ufs/qcom,ufs-common.yaml

```yaml
properties:
  qcom,vddp-ref-clk-supply:
    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
    description: Optional UFS device REF_CLK pad supply.

  qcom,vddp-ref-clk-max-microamp:
    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
    minimum: 1
    description: Maximum current requested from qcom,vddp-ref-clk-supply.

  qcom,vccq-parent-supply:
    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
    description: Optional parent supply for the UFS device VCCQ rail.

  qcom,vccq-parent-max-microamp:
    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
    minimum: 1
    description: Maximum current requested from qcom,vccq-parent-supply.
```

## Known hardware/software limits

- PM8150L S8 SMPS8 uses ACK pmic5_hfsmps510 / rpmh_regulator_vrm_ops. Those
  ops have no DRMS set_load/get_optimum_mode callback. The 210 mA request
  may be accepted without an actual mode change; regulator_enable still
  has a hardware implementation.
- PM8150 L6 LDO6 is already the generic vccq-supply provider and also the
  separate VDDP reference-clock pad supply. The regulator framework tracks
  consumer enables and loads separately. The HOS4.3 local map gives VDDP
  max load 100 uA; its provider output is fixed at 1.2 V.
- The current ACK QMP UFS PHY bulk regulator list for SM8250 contains only
  vdda-phy and vdda-pll. Do not put qcom,vddp-ref-clk-supply in &ufs_mem_phy.
- The ACK UFS driver must consume both vendor properties; DTS alone is inert.
- Dummy-regulator fallback can still mask an unresolved PMIC physical input
  supply. Neither S8 nor L6 electrical input paths are proven by this patch.
- This patch sketch is not a verified apply-ready diff. No compile or boot
  testing has been performed.
